{"pages": [{"id": 676065, "key": "Type_59_tank", "title": "Type 59 tank", "excerpt": "The <span class=\"searchmatch\">Type</span> 59 (Chinese: 59式; pinyin: Wǔ jiǔ shì; industrial designation: WZ-120) is a Chinese version of the Soviet T-54A main battle <span class=\"searchmatch\">tank</span>, an early model", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "Chinese main battle tank", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/jpeg", "width": 60, "height": 45, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Type_59_tank_in_Military_Museum_of_the_Chinese_People%27s_Revolution_20180219.jpg/60px-Type_59_tank_in_Military_Museum_of_the_Chinese_People%27s_Revolution_20180219.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}, {"id": 6918851, "key": "Japanese_tanks_of_World_War_II", "title": "Japanese tanks of World War II", "excerpt": "produced <span class=\"searchmatch\">tanks</span>. Then in 1930 they were able to acquire ten examples of its <span class=\"searchmatch\">successor</span>, the Renault NC1 (designated Otsu-Gata Sensha or &quot;<span class=\"searchmatch\">Type</span> B <span class=\"searchmatch\">Tank</span>&quot;). Both", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/jpeg", "width": 60, "height": 47, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Chi-Nu_4th_Tank_Division.JPG/60px-Chi-Nu_4th_Tank_Division.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}, {"id": 1199188, "key": "Panhard_ERC", "title": "Panhard ERC", "excerpt": "large-scale production: the ERC-<span class=\"searchmatch\">90</span> Lynx and the ERC-<span class=\"searchmatch\">90</span> Sagaie. The main difference between the two versions is the <span class=\"searchmatch\">type</span> of turret and <span class=\"searchmatch\">90</span> mm gun fitted. Sagaie is", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "French armored car", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/jpeg", "width": 60, "height": 40, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/ERC-90_Sagaie_008_FR.JPG/60px-ERC-90_Sagaie_008_FR.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}, {"id": 68012478, "key": "T25_medium_tank", "title": "T25 medium tank", "excerpt": "possible replacement for both the M4 Sherman Medium <span class=\"searchmatch\">tank</span>, and its previously proposed <span class=\"searchmatch\">successor</span>, the T23. Designed between mid-1943 and early 1944, the", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "T25 Medium tank prototype", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/jpeg", "width": 60, "height": 33, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/T25.jpg/60px-T25.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}, {"id": 28765229, "key": "Tanks_of_China", "title": "Tanks of China", "excerpt": "new welded turret and 125 mm autoloaded <span class=\"searchmatch\">tank</span> gun. The <span class=\"searchmatch\">Type</span> 80 and <span class=\"searchmatch\">Type</span> 85 <span class=\"searchmatch\">tanks</span> led to the <span class=\"searchmatch\">Type</span> <span class=\"searchmatch\">90</span>. The <span class=\"searchmatch\">Type</span> <span class=\"searchmatch\">90</span> was rejected for Chinese service in favour", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/jpeg", "width": 60, "height": 38, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/ZTZ-96_MBT_20131004.JPG/60px-ZTZ-96_MBT_20131004.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}, {"id": 1162899, "key": "90_mm_gun_M1/M2/M3", "title": "90 mm gun M1/M2/M3", "excerpt": "The <span class=\"searchmatch\">90</span> mm gun M1/M2/M3 was an American heavy anti-aircraft and anti-<span class=\"searchmatch\">tank</span> gun, playing a role similar to the German 8.8cm Flak 18. It had a 3.5 in (<span class=\"searchmatch\">90</span> mm)", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "Type of anti-aircraft gun and anti-tank gun (M1, M2) and tank gun (M3)", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/jpeg", "width": 60, "height": 31, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/90mm_M1_AAgun_CFB_Borden.jpg/60px-90mm_M1_AAgun_CFB_Borden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}]}